    "body": "## Summary\n\nClamp the QSA mapped-token count to `num_actual_tokens` in both Triton and Torch metadata builders. Graph capture may pad `query_start_loc_cpu[-1]` beyond the real token count, while QSA metadata buffers only contain real tokens. Without the clamp, metadata construction can read or write past those buffers during padded decode.\n\nAdd a CPU regression test with one real decode token and three graph-padding slots. The test checks the real token request mapping, logical position, visible block count, and slot mapping.\n\n## Validation\n\n- QSA CPU regression selection in the existing A3 test container: 8 passed (including the original padded-decode test on the same implementation and related QSA tests).\n- The new four-offset regression scenario was executed directly against the patched Torch builder and returned the expected metadata `[0], [2400], [2401], [0]`.\n- `compileall` and `git diff --check` passed.\n\nCUDA/Triton execution was not available in this A3 environment; the equivalent Triton bound change is included but requires CUDA CI coverage.\n\nSigned-off-by: shaopeng-666 <217884671+shaopeng-666@users.noreply.github.com>",
